3244334a-af52-49d8-b847-8f5b1389916b	2026-05-23 01:58:36.676507	2026-05-23 03:02:36.676507	Technical Interview - Senior Frontend Engineer position with Leila Bennani	https://zoom.us/j/167885958	2026-06-11 01:58:36.676507	Good cultural fit, needs technical assessment follow-up	12	64	abfc1957-d86c-4912-ba5e-8fe16afd9671	e599e6b0-211a-4792-a32b-d5b339a0a606	1d4d1c5e-211e-4e3b-aed7-1f0424f53099	["AI - 00:07:00 : How do you ensure the **security** of the code you write from a high-level perspective? || Candidate - 00:04:30 : I aim to transition into a **Principal or Lead Architect** role, focusing on designing highly available, multi-region cloud systems, specifically leveraging serverless technologies and advanced networking on AWS or Azure.", "AI - 00:14:00 : How do you ensure the **security** of the code you write from a high-level perspective? || Candidate - 00:05:30 : Security is a layered approach. I start with **OWASP Top 10** checks, use static analysis tools in the pipeline, and ensure all input is validated and sanitized, following the principle of least privilege in access controls.", "AI - 00:10:00 : How do you manage configuration secrets and credentials in a **Kubernetes** environment? || Candidate - 00:18:30 : Polymorphism allows objects of different classes to be treated as objects of a common type. A good example is using a list of a parent class type to hold various sub-class objects and iterating through them.", "AI - 00:14:00 : Describe your experience with **CI/CD pipelines** using tools like Jenkins or GitLab CI. || Candidate - 00:04:30 : Message brokers are vital for **decoupling services** and handling asynchronous communication, ensuring reliability for tasks like order fulfillment or notification processing, which don't require immediate synchronous confirmation.", "AI - 00:13:00 : Walk me through the lifecycle of a **Spring bean** and point out where dependency injection occurs. || Candidate - 00:08:30 : Indexing significantly speeds up search queries on large tables but slows down writes (INSERT/UPDATE). I index columns frequently used in `WHERE` clauses, `ORDER BY`, or `JOIN` conditions, but avoid over-indexing, especially on low-cardinality columns.", "AI - 00:08:00 : Explain how **Garbage Collection** works in the JVM and what Generational Garbage Collection achieves. || Candidate - 00:04:30 : A **JOIN** is a standard SQL operation to combine columns from two or more rows based on a related column. An **ACID transaction** is a fundamental concept guaranteeing that database operations are reliable and complete as a single unit.", "AI - 00:20:00 : How do you optimize slow-running database queries and identify bottlenecks? || Candidate - 00:05:30 : I use a **service mesh** like Istio or Consul for automated service discovery, coupled with Round Robin or Least Connections algorithms for traffic distribution at the ingress level.", "AI - 00:20:00 : Explain the concept of **indexing** in a relational database and how to decide which columns to index. || Candidate - 00:03:30 : TDD forces me to think about the **contract and interface** before implementation. It results in code that is inherently more testable, modular, and leads to fewer production bugs because the requirements are enshrined in automated tests.", "AI - 00:14:00 : How do you optimize slow-running database queries and identify bottlenecks? || Candidate - 00:05:30 : I dealt with a monolithic banking system using Java 6 and legacy EJBs. My approach was to implement an **anti-corruption layer** around key business domains, allowing us to slowly extract services into a modern framework without halting feature development.", "AI - 00:10:00 : What is the difference between a **JOIN and an ACID transaction** in PostgreSQL? || Candidate - 00:04:30 : Polymorphism allows objects of different classes to be treated as objects of a common type. A good example is using a list of a parent class type to hold various sub-class objects and iterating through them.", "AI - 00:19:00 : What is the primary difference between **IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS**, and which do you prefer for application deployment? || Candidate - 00:13:30 : Indexing significantly speeds up search queries on large tables but slows down writes (INSERT/UPDATE). I index columns frequently used in `WHERE` clauses, `ORDER BY`, or `JOIN` conditions, but avoid over-indexing, especially on low-cardinality columns.", "AI - 00:20:00 : Explain how **Garbage Collection** works in the JVM and what Generational Garbage Collection achieves. || Candidate - 00:10:30 : I use a **shadow database strategy** or **logical replication**. For shadow databases, the new schema is built alongside the old, and data is double-written during the transition phase, ensuring seamless cutover.", "AI - 00:14:00 : Describe how you handle large dataset migrations with **zero downtime**. || Candidate - 00:17:30 : I use a **service mesh** like Istio or Consul for automated service discovery, coupled with Round Robin or Least Connections algorithms for traffic distribution at the ingress level.", "AI - 00:13:00 : What are the advantages of using a **message broker** like Kafka or RabbitMQ in a distributed system? || Candidate - 00:13:30 : Indexing significantly speeds up search queries on large tables but slows down writes (INSERT/UPDATE). I index columns frequently used in `WHERE` clauses, `ORDER BY`, or `JOIN` conditions, but avoid over-indexing, especially on low-cardinality columns.", "AI - 00:11:00 : Describe a time you had to **mentor a junior developer** on a complex technical issue. || Candidate - 00:05:30 : I use **Kubernetes Secrets** for sensitive data, coupled with external solutions like HashiCorp Vault or cloud-native key management services for better protection and rotation.", "AI - 00:04:00 : Explain the concept of **indexing** in a relational database and how to decide which columns to index. || Candidate - 00:20:30 : String is immutable, leading to memory overhead with constant concatenation. StringBuilder is faster and mutable but not thread-safe; StringBuffer is thread-safe but slightly slower. I use StringBuilder in single-threaded environments.", "AI - 00:13:00 : Walk me through the lifecycle of a **Spring bean** and point out where dependency injection occurs. || Candidate - 00:01:30 : I start by running an `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` on the query to understand its execution plan, looking for **full table scans** or missing indexes. Often, rewriting a subquery or adjusting an index solves the issue.", "AI - 00:04:00 : What is the difference between a **JOIN and an ACID transaction** in PostgreSQL? || Candidate - 00:10:30 : NoSQL is great for **high-velocity, schema-less data** like session logs or user profiles, offering horizontal scalability. SQL is better when data integrity (ACID) and complex relational querying are non-negotiable requirements.", "AI - 00:07:00 : When scaling microservices, what strategies do you employ for **service discovery and load balancing**? || Candidate - 00:06:30 : The bean lifecycle starts with instantiation, followed by dependency injection (via setters/constructors), initialization callbacks (@PostConstruct), and finally, itÔÇÖs ready for use. It ends with the container closing and destruction callbacks.", "AI - 00:02:00 : What are the performance implications when choosing between **String, StringBuilder, and StringBuffer**? || Candidate - 00:11:30 : I prefer **PaaS (Platform as a Service)**, like AWS Elastic Beanstalk or Azure App Service, as it balances control with productivity, handling the underlying OS/infrastructure updates for me. IaaS is too much manual overhead.", "AI - 00:18:00 : What are the performance implications when choosing between **String, StringBuilder, and StringBuffer**? || Candidate - 00:15:30 : I use a **service mesh** like Istio or Consul for automated service discovery, coupled with Round Robin or Least Connections algorithms for traffic distribution at the ingress level.", "AI - 00:12:00 : How do you ensure the **security** of the code you write from a high-level perspective? || Candidate - 00:03:30 : NoSQL is great for **high-velocity, schema-less data** like session logs or user profiles, offering horizontal scalability. SQL is better when data integrity (ACID) and complex relational querying are non-negotiable requirements.", "AI - 00:07:00 : When scaling microservices, what strategies do you employ for **service discovery and load balancing**? || Candidate - 00:19:30 : Message brokers are vital for **decoupling services** and handling asynchronous communication, ensuring reliability for tasks like order fulfillment or notification processing, which don't require immediate synchronous confirmation.", "AI - 00:19:00 : Describe a time you had to **mentor a junior developer** on a complex technical issue. || Candidate - 00:07:30 : I use a **shadow database strategy** or **logical replication**. For shadow databases, the new schema is built alongside the old, and data is double-written during the transition phase, ensuring seamless cutover.", "AI - 00:17:00 : Describe your experience with **CI/CD pipelines** using tools like Jenkins or GitLab CI. || Candidate - 00:06:30 : I use **Kubernetes Secrets** for sensitive data, coupled with external solutions like HashiCorp Vault or cloud-native key management services for better protection and rotation."]
